YouHexen2 - compiling from source
=================================

YouHexen2 is an Emscripten-only HTML5/WebAssembly target. engine/CMakeLists.txt intentionally rejects native toolchains; there is no current Linux, Windows, SDL, or OpenGL build.

Requirements:

  - Emscripten SDK 4.0.23
  - CMake
  - Node.js 22 or newer for PWA tests

Use the convenience targets from the repository root:

    source "$EMSDK/emsdk_env.sh"

    make build          # WebGlideNitro, the primary native WebGPU renderer
    make build-software # classic 8-bit renderer with WebGPU presentation
    make dist           # build both renderers and assemble the PWA in dist/
    make test           # run the Node-based PWA tests

The Makefile calls the same scripts used by CI, Pages, and release builds:

    ./scripts/wasm-build.sh nitro engine/build-nitro
    ./scripts/wasm-build.sh software
    ./scripts/wasm-assemble-artifact.sh dist
    ./scripts/wasm-validate-artifact.sh dist

WEB_RENDERER is the only renderer selector:

  webgpu   WebGlideNitro; defines WEBGPUQUAKE and emits hexenwail-nitro.*
  software classic rasterizer; defines WEBSOFT and emits hexenwail.*

The inherited hexenwail bundle names are stable internal identifiers. See web/ARCHITECTURE.md for the complete platform and macro contract and PWA.md for local serving and deployment.
